Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the solution:

## Solution

I implemented the `tokenize` function in `src/diff.js`. The function converts a split text (from `splitLines`) into tokens that remember whether each line had a newline terminator.

**Key insight:** 
- Lines in the middle of a text always had newline terminators (they were separated by `\n`)
- Only the last line's termination status depends on whether the original text ended with a newline

**Implementation:**
```javascript
function tokenize(split) {
  const tokens = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < split.lines.length; i += 1) {
    const isLastLine = i === split.lines.length - 1;
    const terminated = isLastLine ? split.newlineAtEnd : true;
    tokens.push({ text: split.lines[i], terminated });
  }
  return tokens;
